Z||000007||qwikgta||06-26-2001||09:46 PM||||Next to some 355 kits, this is my fav too.  But since day one I have always said that the rear end just does not look right, something about the "cutout" or "recess" area around the backside of the wheel.  I agree the rear end needs some work for me, the front is kick a$$ and I also like the fino mid-rear end treetment.  Maybe someday someone will get one and make a change to the rearend that others can copy.  IMO<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000008||Archie||06-26-2001||11:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR><B> Exactly what I was thinking, those tail lights have to go!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> I would like to see something like a late 90's Trans Am rear end, something more muscular.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The beauty of doing a re-body that is not a replica of a Ferrari or something is that you can make changes to it to make it your very own unique automobile. When making a "Replica" of another car, you usually try to replicate all if it's features, even the features you don't like.<P>Every since I bought Candy Apple Cars, I've looked at a lot of tail lights while driving down the road. If you look around a bit you'll find that there are several cars which have tallights that would work well with these cars.<P>Some of the guys on this forum are pretty good with editing photos. Maybe we can take some pics. of various tail lights and "plug" them into the back of a Fino.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||06-26-2001||11:55 PM||||Personally, I love the Finale just the way it is.. If I could afford it, my T-top would become a Finale instead of a fastback Indy clone... Run a sale, Archie! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
