Z||000014||Monkeyman||06-27-2001||05:25 AM||||underdog--Sure they could be cheaper, but...There's alot going into a kit.  You have to recover the cost of either R & D or purchasing the molds, labor to make each kit, assemble same (put all the parts into the same box), etc.  Then there's the profit factor.  Archie (as well as all the rest) is in this business to make money (I'm guessing this is his only means of income, but I didn't ask).  He has to decide how much money he wants to clear when he sells a kit.  I don't even know how much the kits sell for (personally I want one of AusFieros "kits" when he makes them--sorry Archie <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), but it's probably in line with what you can get elsewhere.  <P>This is not a plug for Archie.  I don't know the man nor have I ever purchased anything from him (no way I can afford a SBC) although I don't have anything against him, either.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||06-27-2001||03:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by underdog:<BR><B>i definately dont want to be mean, but couldnt the kits be a lot cheaper? they cant be too expensive to produce after a mold is made. especially if there was more sales of them, they could be a lot cheaper, no? maybe there is a good reason, but i fail to see it i guess</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cars are probably only about $2k worth of steel, glass, rubber, carpet, etc. why charge $20k+ for them?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
