Z||000025||Archie||06-27-2001||10:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>I just realized the Finales have that vent too..<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The center vent is a personal item we thought would look good on the back end. Kinda optional, another thing you can do to personalize your Finale or Fino. I'm not using it ont the 2 cars we have in process now. NOW, I think it looks better without it.<P>The vents around the rear clip do in fact aid in venting the engine compartment. I guarantee that the engine compartments in the Fino & Finale are a lot cooler than any stock bodied Fiero.<P>The Blue car with the Miata tail lights was at the Daytona show last year. Another way to personalize your car. Note how the Miata light curves to match the body lines. <P>Miata lights look pretty good however, when they are turned on, they have only one tail light bulb. IMHO, I think the cars need more than one little bulb lit up across the back of the car.<P>Next time you are driving around town, look at the tail lights of the car in front of you & remembering the contour of the Fino/Finale body think of which lights would look cool in that car.<P>Besides, looking at tail lights is a lot safer than looking at the girls walking down to the beach.<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
